  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Western Hemisphere Regional Processing Center Capacity and Infrastructure</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In April 2023, the Government of the United States of America (US) announced new measures that will form part of its revised migration policy, including efforts to limit the flow of irregular migrants across the southern Mexico-US border. This will be achieved through, among other initiatives, expanding access to refugee resettlement and other lawful pathways for eligible individuals from Cuba, Haiti, Nicaragua, Venezuela, Guatemala, El Salvador and Honduras. IOM is working along with UNHCR to provide counselling assistance in order for interested migrants and refugees to access reliable information on their potential eligibility to available pathways such as resettlement, humanitarian parole and family reunification.</narrative>
  </description>
